WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.586
Attachment is personal work.

00:00:01.586 --> 00:00:04.758
Put ideas on a kill or keep sheet.

00:00:04.758 --> 00:00:07.929
This lesson is about personal: idea kill list.

00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:09.119
Attachment: kill/keep sheet.

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:11.894
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.894 --> 00:00:15.859
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:21.806
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:26.167
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:30.528
Stay practical: complete kill/keep sheet before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:33.614
For each idea: keep, kill, or park.

00:00:33.614 --> 00:00:36.774
Add one evidence note so romance cannot hide.

00:00:36.774 --> 00:00:39.145
Remember the objective: complete kill/keep sheet.

00:00:39.145 --> 00:00:43.490
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:48.231
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:48.231 --> 00:00:52.577
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:52.577 --> 00:00:57.318
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:57.318 --> 00:01:00.084
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:00.084 --> 00:01:01.664
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:05.222
Complete the kill/keep sheet before you start Offer.

00:01:05.222 --> 00:01:06.842
Clarity here saves weeks.

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:09.270
Remember the objective: complete kill/keep sheet.

